From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 03:38:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10596/11171] Name the test that overwrites a tracked artifact
 on every full-suite run

Caught live while a conductor child ran the full suite: git status showed
results/experiment_1822_rtl_synth.log modified. The Test-Run Record Integrity
Discipline predicted this class; this entry supplies the culprit.

test_experiment_1822_rtl_synth.py::test_req_hw_056_synth_constraints shells out to
`make synth-constraints`, whose recipe hardcodes the output path
`> results/experiment_1822_rtl_synth.log`. The test cannot redirect it, so every
full-suite run re-runs yosys over a tracked historical log.

No damage this time, by luck rather than design: the logfile hash is identical
(1855ef30ab), so the synthesis result is unchanged and only wall-clock timings and
peak memory moved. A toolchain change would rewrite the substance just as silently.

The entry carries the fix -- parameterise the recipe's output directory and have
the test pass tmp_path -- plus a trap found while writing it. The test asserts on
results/experiment_1822_rtl_synth.json, which this recipe never writes, so that
assertion currently passes against a checked-in file the test did not produce.
Pointing the test at tmp_path will expose it, and both need fixing together or the
test goes red for a second unrelated reason.

Not fixed here: the suite was running through that Makefile target at the time.
Editing a recipe mid-run risks a confusing failure that would land in the
conductor's own FAIL count. It belongs between runs, the same call made earlier
tonight about the eval's per-game write.

Two other observations from the window, both checked and benign. The GPU reaper
logged SKIP protected server for the live llama-server, so that protection works.
Two gitea push failures looked like a mirror outage until counted: exactly 2 in 2
days, both inside one 21-second window, and all five outer-loop commits are present
on the canonical remote.

